592186459221 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $p=⟨5,-2,2⟩,$ $q=⟨3,k,1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-8,3,-4⟩$ are coplanar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2eedb023-f05d-5365-a7fb-580375aea9cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1074 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & k & 1 \\\\ -8 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -8 & -4\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(k\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot (-4)-(-8)\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot 3-(-8)\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-20k-15-8+18+16k \\\\  & =-4k-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ -4k-5 & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{5}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42055" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-1,2,5⟩$, $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$ and $c=⟨0,5,1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8fcc06ee-9e96-5a19-8006-dabebc81e1fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-((-4)\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 2)-2(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)+5(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =14-2+25 \\\\  & =37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|37|=37.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1069 "q-20144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(3,-2,2)$, $B(4,3,2)$, $C(1,3,5)$, $D(2,4,-6).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da5d7cb9-5c27-5b41-96e4-8767d3252a54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+2k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+3j+5k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+5j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,5,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+4j-6k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+6j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-1,6,-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -8\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -8\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5\\cdot (-8)-6\\cdot 3)-5((-2)\\cdot (-8)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+0 \\\\  & =-58-95 \\\\  & =-153.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-153|=153.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483606 #edb/ref 1080 "28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483606 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483606 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17336941-881c-5fb2-a109-5b4a5addcfec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484039 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{16}{13}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484039 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484039 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eea5ea1b-1584-5bf8-9c56-60e082cc3b30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484042 #edb/ref 1080 "22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484042 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484042 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ef21b691-d97c-5047-bd55-f0d2f57c360d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484137 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484137 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484137 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484137 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186484042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484137 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "752c7d24-ba0b-5853-99e8-14fd968c0d02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484164 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186483606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484164 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484164 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484164 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186483606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484164 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a6a81b1b-3ad2-556f-aea1-11eab91bed3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484170 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186484039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484170 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484170 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484170 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186484039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484170 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aefbe563-901b-5005-9895-d7c05a2acfbf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484224 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484224 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280714" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484224 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484224 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $p=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $q=⟨0,5,1⟩$, and $r=⟨4,0,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484224 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "54f335de-9889-5585-819e-c5ae71a53628" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484224 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(30)-2(0\\cdot 6-1\\cdot 4)+3(0\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =30+8-60 \\\\  & =-22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-22|=22.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484229 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484229 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280747" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484229 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484229 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨2,k,-1⟩$, $b=⟨-3,4,5⟩$, and $c=⟨6,k,1⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484229 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "65ad1da6-49b7-5494-8267-2eea67ec5389" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484229 #edb/ref 1074 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & k & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & k & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ k & 1\\end{aligned}|-k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 1-5\\cdot k)-k(-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 6)-1(-3\\cdot k-4\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =8-10k+33k+3k+24 \\\\  & =26k+32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 26k+32 & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{16}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{16}{13}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484248 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484248 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280669" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484248 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484248 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨3,0,-2⟩$, $y=⟨1,2,4⟩$, and $z=⟨-5,1,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484248 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8951c125-ece2-55e4-a6b5-7a7f9b036e1d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484248 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 1)+0+(-2)(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-5)) \\\\  & =-6-22 \\\\  & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-28|=28.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
